; https://github.com/paijp/vps-subdomain-mcp
;
; Operator-managed DNS records for one domain (multidomain edition).
; Copy to <your-domain>.dns, edit, then run:  make <your-domain>.dnsdone
; Re-run after every edit; delete a line and re-run to delete a record.
;
; Names are relative to the domain (@ = the domain itself).
; The host adds SOA, NS, ns1 A and DKIM (mail._domainkey) — do not write
; those. It also adds defaults for @ A, * A, the @ / * SPF TXT and the
; _dmarc TXT; writing one of these here replaces that default (e.g. point
; the apex at another server, or keep an existing SPF). No A/AAAA/CNAME on
; names served by a container, except an A record with this host's own IP
; (write one where the wildcard does not answer, i.e. for a container name
; that has records below it: "iot0 IN A <host IP>" when "http.iot0" exists) or,
; while that container is in forward mode, with the old server's IP.
; Every record line must start with its owner name (no leading whitespace).

; @       IN MX    10 mail.example.net.
; @       IN TXT   "google-site-verification=xxxxxxxx"
; docs    IN CNAME ghs.googlehosted.com.
; @       IN A     192.0.2.10                       ; apex on another server
; @       IN TXT   "v=spf1 a:mail.example.net mx ~all"  ; own SPF instead of the default
